          "case_name": "Matter of Termination of Parental Rights to ALRW",
          "citation": "2023 WY 20, 525 P.3d 627",
          "court": "Wyoming Supreme Court",
          "year": 2023,
          "date_decided": "2023-03-10",
          "holding": "The Court affirmed termination under Wyo. Stat. Ann. § 14-2-309(a)(iii), holding that the sufficiency of the Department's reasonable efforts is assessed case by case and that the Department must tie its efforts to the reasons that necessitated the child's out-of-home placement.",
          "relevance": "Case-by-case judicial review of reasonable efforts is the state-court analogue of federal CFSR scrutiny.",
          "quote": "We assess whether sufficient evidence supports that DFS made reasonable efforts to rehabilitate the family on a case-by-case basis",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/9382982/in-the-matter-of-the-termination-of-parental-rights-to-alrw-minor-child/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 9382982
        },
        {
          "case_name": "Matter of Termination of Parental Rights to PML and EGL",
          "citation": "2024 WY 37, 545 P.3d 856",
          "court": "Wyoming Supreme Court",
          "year": 2024,
          "date_decided": "2024-04-01",
          "holding": "The Court affirmed termination, holding that whether the Department made reasonable efforts is assessed case by case, that its efforts must be accessible and tailored to the parent, and that a case plan adapted to a mother's intellectual disability satisfied the standard.",
          "relevance": "Judicial case-by-case review of agency effort is the state check corresponding to federal permanency monitoring.",
          "quote": "We assess on a case-by-case basis whether sufficient evidence exists to demonstrate the Department made reasonable efforts to rehabilitate the family",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/9489606/in-the-matter-of-the-termination-of-parental-rights-to-pml-and-egl-minor/",
